{"case":902,"commit":"8157af8b331ded1534c033efac6720f4f738a131","event":"ruling","failed_agent":null,"failure_reason":null,"findings":0,"hash":"8fb97ca5fcd618253574a8c955e0105294def5bb0b37d2f849dfdd9f61c3e611","invocation":"20261013T173145.097228+0000-50808","prev":"ad5319e76c3e9c65381d17a87730ba9ba641c01ff04cafa7c6cc7ab4e9a07c57","prompts":"22632cd34844e0081074113a839ba6ace2b861ccd53624978403e6b8c0e1f3d5","ruling":{"amount_sgd":3.44,"confidence":0.85,"driver_compensation_sgd":null,"explanation":"To both parties: the rider's fare is partly returned, and the amount is fixed by the route-deviation policy, not by the difference between the quoted and the charged fare.\n\nWhat is established. The platform's own trip record (EV-TRIP-00902, complete at weight 1.0) records 24.8 km driven against 20.5 km on the recommended Orchard Central - Changi T3 route. Under POL-RD-22 the deviation is that subtraction: 4.30 km, well outside the 1.0 km tolerance. POL-RD-22 does not re-measure the route from the GPS trace (EV-GPS-00902 is impaired at weight 0.8 on LOW_SAMPLE_RATE; a sparse trace understates a route's length), so the trace is not relied on and its impairment does not enter this ruling.\n\nThe reroute was traffic-justified. TC-001 (EV-ADVIS-00902-01) records a HIGH-severity vehicle fire on the PIE eastbound with lanes 1 and 2 blocked, intersecting the recommended route and inside the trip window, and TC-002 (EV-ADVIS-00902-02) records heavy congestion at the PIE's Changi Airport exit ramp over the same window. Both are of the kinds POL-RD-23 names (incident, congestion) and both intersect the route and overlap the trip. The driver was entitled to reroute (POL-RD-21).\n\nThe driver did not inform the rider. The complete, contiguous chat log (EV-CHAT-00902, weight 1.0) contains no message announcing a route change: the driver's only messages before the rider's query are pre-trip pleasantries (13:09, 13:10:30). The rider raises the route herself at 13:24 ('are we going the right way?'), and the driver's 13:25 reply, 'Don't worry, I know the way. We will reach on time.', names no deviation and gives no reason, so it is not the notice POL-RD-21 requires. No call recording exists. That makes the driver's notification the only open question to test.\n\nOn the refund matrix. The case is POL-RD-24 row (b): traffic-justified, rider not informed, deviation over 1 km. The measure is the excess distance fare: 4.30 km x 0.80 SGD per km (EV-FARE-00902) = 3.44 SGD, with no surge. That is why the rider's figure of 6.50 SGD is not awarded: the policy's route-deviation refund is the excess distance fare (POL-RD-24), not the 35.00 charged less the 28.50 quote. The driver's own submission to the same effect is accepted. Row (d) (not traffic-justified) would pay the same 3.44 SGD, so nothing turns on which justification branch applies.\n\nWhy this is not escalated. The driver argues that because a verbal notice at the wheel leaves no record, 'whether the driver notified the rider' cannot be established and POL-GEN-26 requires human review, or alternatively that the driver's 13:25 reply was notice to a rider who objected (POL-RD-24's catch-all). Neither succeeds. The evidence that carries the notification fact - the chat log - is present, complete and unimpaired; it shows no notice, so the fact is established in the negative rather than missing. POL-RD-21 makes an unrecorded verbal notice incapable of satisfying the driver's obligation, and the driver here asserted none (no counterparty statement on file). Reading every no-notice case as unestablished would make row (b), the clause's own provision for exactly this situation, a dead letter. The catch-all does not apply because the driver never informed the rider in the first place.\n\nConfidence and authority. POL-RD-25 requires 0.80 and the deciding facts rest on artifacts all at weight 1.0 (trip record, chat log, fare ledger, both route advisories), so the cap allows 0.85. The value in dispute, 6.50 SGD, is below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, neither profile carries a fraud flag, there is no safety flag, and POL-RD-25's 2 km AI limit is not applied on this version, so the AI ruling is final and the refund issues rather than the charge being held. No clause of the route-deviation policy produces a referral on these facts.\n\nThe judge was asked 4 times on the same inputs and every draft agreed on this ruling, so it is carried unanimously (vote agreement 1.00).","referrals":[],"ruling":"PARTIAL_REFUND"},"seq":38,"ts":"2026-10-13T17:36:07.805275+00:00"}
